Third-party code under third_party/
===================================

Two frameworks are included as git submodules. They are not part of this repository's own code
and stay under their own licenses. Each license text is the LICENSE file in its submodule directory.

  OpenClaw-RL   https://github.com/Gen-Verse/OpenClaw-RL   Apache License 2.0
                commit f48ac358adf9873b5cb2210f1cb234a52ed8a8a3
  MetaClaw      https://github.com/aiming-lab/MetaClaw     MIT License
                commit 922caf3a1cd093fb316e95183a8acc8aa47b3b21

Patches
-------

The patches in this directory modify three source files of these frameworks:

  openclaw-rl-rollout.patch      OpenClaw-RL   openclaw-tinker/rollout.py
  metaclaw-skill-evolver.patch   MetaClaw      metaclaw/skill_evolver.py
  metaclaw-api-server.patch      MetaClaw      metaclaw/api_server.py

A patch quotes lines of the file it changes, so it remains under the license of that file: the
Apache License 2.0 for the OpenClaw-RL patch, the MIT License for the two MetaClaw patches. The
license of this repository does not replace them for these files. The OpenClaw-RL patch adds a
comment to the file it changes, stating that the file was modified.

`python -m evolve_ipi.thirdparty apply` applies the patches to the working trees of the submodules.
It changes no commit of either framework. SHA256SUMS holds the sha256 that each patched file must
have afterwards, and `python -m evolve_ipi.thirdparty verify` checks it.
